# s2b-ops core wiring

## 1. Modules
mixdog-connections/src/lib.rs already lists `pub mod cleanup_ops; pub mod diagnostics_ops; pub mod host_list_ops;`. Add the tests after `mod stores_tests;`:
```
#[cfg(test)]
mod ops_tests;
```

## 2. Cargo
No new dependency edge: the modules use mixdog-ssh, mixdog-core-api, mixdog-app-protocol, mixdog-rt, async-trait, serde_json and tracing, all already in
mixdog-connections/Cargo.toml (tests: tempfile, tokio, mixdog-rt test-support).

## 3. SERVICE_PENDING (mixdog-app-server-daemon compose_flip.rs)
These modules serve no protocol method by themselves. The service (s2b-service) serves these with the functions below and removes them from SERVICE_PENDING:
`connections/ssh/list`, `connections/ssh/rename`, `connections/ssh/forget`, `connections/ssh/updateSettings`, `connections/ssh/cleanup`,
`connections/ssh/diagnosticsLog`, `connections/ssh/diagnosticsCopy`, `connections/ssh/serverLog`.

## 4. For the service wiring (s2b-service)
- `HostList::new(hosts, link_pool as Arc<dyn HostLinks>)` (`LinkPool` implements `HostLinks`, which extends `ServerLinks`):
  list -> `list()`; rename{id,name} -> `rename(&id,&name)` (empty result); forget{id} -> `forget(&id)` (empty result);
  updateSettings{id,settings} -> `update_settings(&id,&settings_json)` (answers the `SshHost`; the model login change reaches the live link on its own task).
  `AttemptError` is the request error (its Display text is the message).
- `Cleanup::new(CleanupDeps { hosts, attempts: connect.attempts().clone(), cleaner: Arc::new(EnvCleaner { env: ssh_env, payloads }), login })`, `login` and `attempts`
  being the instances `Connect` was built with, `payloads` the owned `ServerPayloads` the `LinkPool` got. cleanup{id, operationId, removeUserData, forget} ->
  `cleanup(caller, &id, request, sink)`; `sink` sends the `connections/ssh/cleanupProgress` notification (`@connection`) to the caller. The questions of ssh
  arrive as `connections/ssh/askpass` with `attemptId` = the operationId and are answered by `connections/ssh/askpassReply` like a connect attempt's.
- `DiagnosticsOps::new(hosts, Arc::new(EnvDiagnostics { env: ssh_env, os_release }))`; `os_release` is the OS release string the report prints (Windows
  `10.0.26100`, the same text mixdog-core's host_info reads). diagnosticsLog / diagnosticsCopy / serverLog -> `log` / `copy` / `server_log` with the asker:
  `Asker::ThisPc` when the caller is the main window, `Asker::Server(connection_id)` when it is a server window (policy.rs already limits the caller to M or S).
  `copy` takes the app version from the caller's `initialize` clientInfo.version (the caller's own, never a global).
- `connect::host_settings` and `restore::attempt_context` build the ssh context of a saved server; cleanup and server-log run inside it (batch mode first, askpass on retry).
